224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (human and artificial intelligence \(AI\). In particular, I study AI that is socially interactive \(e.g., robots, chatbots\) to better understand how people perceive and engage with these agents, including in human-AI teams. Much of my work in also explores how individual differences affect collaborative relationships and AI perception. Before coming to Purdue, I was an Assistant Professor at the University of Oklahoma and a postdoc in the School of Communication at Northwestern University. I completed my Ph.D. in I/O at the University of Georgia and earned by my B.A. in psychology from St. Olaf College in Northfield, Minnesota. When not working, I enjoy cooking and baking, playing games with family and friends, and trying to keep my dog out of trouble.       Email: aharrisw@purdue.edu)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
